Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:06:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 065/154] feat(atrium): capture the day's lane work in the
 Chromium checkout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

165 files from many parallel lanes lived only in this working tree, so every UAT
task's evidence rested on a state nobody else could reproduce and the patch
series could not regenerate. This captures them as one stack.

Surfaces that became real rather than merely built:
- The Courtyard: a full-window activatable widget hosting a /courtyard page,
  with room cards, click to enter, cross-space tab drag and the two read-only
  lenses. It reused atrium_core_move_tab_to_space rather than adding an ABI verb.
- Pinch to the Courtyard, recognised once in the browser process for both the
  magnify and ctrl+wheel paths. Surface JS was the wrong home: swipe.js already
  owns the wheel and ignores ctrlKey, and a pinch over a page body reaches no
  surface WebContents.
- The sidebar address bar. Bare words go through the real omnibox path,
  AutocompleteInput plus FixupURL, not a hand-rolled heuristic.
- Both sidebar context menus, in the lab's full ordering, with entries whose
  actions do not exist yet visibly disabled rather than inert.
- The AI backends: Ollama and a BYOK custom endpoint, both on Chromium's own
  network stack with redirects refused. The custom endpoint's SSRF guard runs
  before any ResourceRequest exists, so refusal is strictly pre-connect, and the
  keychain key reaches one Authorization header and no log. Ollama is exempt on
  purpose, because reaching your own machine is the point of it.

Thirteen built-but-unwired paths were found and fixed while doing this, always
the same shape: a mechanism built, a test calling it directly, no production
caller, every gate green, feature dead. SetBackdropTint had no caller so the AI
panel's ink never followed a space switch. SummarizeViaOllama had none. A
handler was registered nowhere, which crashes the browser at startup. A data
push ran before its receiver mounted and was dropped, so no non-default Overview
section could show data.

Gates at the time of this commit: cpp-test 450/450, webui-test 995/995, all
three drift guards green, ABI at 24 with both pinned tests current.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
